  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are NNN cans lying on the X-axis at points XiX_iXi​ (1≤i≤N)(1 \\le i \\le N)(1≤i≤N). Each of the N cans is associated with two values AiA_iAi​ and BiB_iBi​.  Also, the segment between the points LLL and RRR (L≤R)(L \\leq R)(L≤R) is considered to be green zone including the points LLL and RRR.\nThere are two types of operations -\n\n1.1.1. Select a can iii out of the NNN cans and move it one unit in either direction along the axis, i.e. if before the operation can is at XiX_iXi​ then after the operation, it moves to either Xi+1X_i+1Xi​+1 or Xi−1X_i-1Xi​−1. This costs BiB_iBi​ coins and it can be performed any number of times for each of the cans.\n\n2.2.2. Choose any integer kkk and shift the green zone to the segment between L′L'L′ and R′R'R′, where L′L'L′ and R′R'R′ are the mirror images of points RRR and LLL with respect to line X=kX=kX=k respectively. This operation should be performed **exactly** once.\n\nAfter all the operations, you get number of coins equal to sum of values of AiA_iAi​ of the cans which lie in the final green zone.\nWe define the net coins as:\n\nNumber&nbsp;of&nbsp;coins&nbsp;you&nbsp;get&nbsp;-&nbsp;Number&nbsp;of&nbsp;coins&nbsp;spent\\texttt{Number of coins you get - Number of coins spent}Number&nbsp;of&nbsp;coins&nbsp;you&nbsp;get&nbsp;-&nbsp;Number&nbsp;of&nbsp;coins&nbsp;spent\n\nFind the **maximum** possible net coins you can earn.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, number of testcases. Then the testcases follow.\nEach of the testcases consists of four lines.\nFirst lines consists of three integers NNN, LLL and RRR.\nNext line consist of NNN space separated integers X1,X2,...,XNX_1, X_2, ..., X_NX1​,X2​,...,XN​.\nNext line consist of NNN space separated integers A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2, ..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​.\nNext line consist of NNN space separated integers B1,B2,...,BNB_1, B_2, ..., B_NB1​,B2​,...,BN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase, output in a single integer, the maximum number of net coins you can earn.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤N≤3⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 3\\cdot 10^51≤N≤3⋅105",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤1091 \\leq A_i, B_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​,Bi​≤109",
      "−109≤L≤R≤109-10^9 \\leq L \\leq  R \\leq 10^9−109≤L≤R≤109",
      "−109≤Xi≤109 -10^9 \\leq X_i \\leq 10^9−109≤Xi​≤109",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 3⋅1053\\cdot 10^53⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n1 7 10\n2\n6\n1\n3 7 10\n2 8 1\n6 20 1\n1 3 2",
        "output": "6\n22",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111 : Lets choose the axis at X=5X=5X=5 and Shift the green zone in the range [0,3][0,3][0,3], such that can lies in green zone. So, there is no need for operation of type 111 and total number of coins earned is A1A_1A1​, i.e. 666.\nTest case 222 : Choose the axis at X=8X=8X=8, so the new green zone lies in the region [6,9][6,9][6,9]. Move the can 111 to X=6X=6X=6. Number of coins received is equal to A1+A2A_1+A_2A1​+A2​ and number of coins spent is 4⋅B14\\cdot B_14⋅B1​. So, the net coins earned is 20+6−4=2220+6-4=2220+6−4=22. This is also the maximum possible."
      }
    ]
